## 📉 Predictive Analytics Page

Here's the complete Streamlit code snippet for your Predictive Analytics page:

```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np

# Placeholder Data (replace with actual predictive analytics data retrieval)
predictive_data = pd.DataFrame({
    "Date": pd.date_range(start="2025-05-01", periods=30),
    "Predicted P/L (£)": np.random.uniform(-200, 500, size=30),
    "Actual P/L (£)": np.random.uniform(-150, 450, size=30)
}).set_index("Date")

# Page Title
st.title("📉 Predictive Analytics")

# Predicted vs Actual P/L
st.subheader("Predicted vs Actual P/L")
st.line_chart(predictive_data)

# Error Metrics
predictive_data["Error (£)"] = predictive_data["Actual P/L (£)"] - predictive_data["Predicted P/L (£)"]
st.subheader("Prediction Error Analysis")
st.bar_chart(predictive_data["Error (£)"])

# Insights and Recommendations
average_error = predictive_data["Error (£)"].mean()
st.subheader("Insights")
st.write(f"Average Prediction Error (£): {average_error:.2f}")

if average_error > 0:
    st.warning("Predictions tend to underestimate actual performance.")
elif average_error < 0:
    st.warning("Predictions tend to overestimate actual performance.")
else:
    st.success("Predictions are highly accurate.")
```

